1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:00,550
Part two.

2
00:00:00,962 --> 00:00:02,125
The last money out the door.

3
00:00:02,525 --> 00:00:04,138
Look at who wrote the biggest checks.

4
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:05,000
Nvidia.

5
00:00:05,412 --> 00:00:06,062
Microsoft.

6
00:00:06,475 --> 00:00:06,825
Google.

7
00:00:07,238 --> 00:00:07,750
AMD.

8
00:00:08,162 --> 00:00:08,875
TSMC.

9
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:09,738
Broadcom.

10
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:10,625
Micron.

11
00:00:11,038 --> 00:00:14,500
Together, about twenty-six billion dollars into the IPO.

12
00:00:14,912 --> 00:00:15,500
Notice something?

13
00:00:15,925 --> 00:00:17,488
These are Anthropic's suppliers.

14
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:18,812
In Zitron's view,

15
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,550
they were topping up a customer,

16
00:00:20,925 --> 00:00:22,575
so that customer can keep paying them,

17
00:00:22,962 --> 00:00:24,800
and so early investors could cash out.

18
00:00:25,225 --> 00:00:26,700
That's why he calls it the last money

19
00:00:26,712 --> 00:00:27,312
out the door.

20
00:00:27,725 --> 00:00:29,888
And retail investors who bought near the top,

21
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:32,975
he notes, faced almost immediate losses.

22
00:00:33,412 --> 00:00:35,387
Here's why that matters for everyone else.

23
00:00:35,812 --> 00:00:37,900
The next big AI company in line is

24
00:00:37,912 --> 00:00:38,588
OpenAI.

25
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,012
It just raised eleven billion dollars,

26
00:00:41,212 --> 00:00:43,438
at a one point two five trillion dollar

27
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:44,113
valuation.

28
00:00:44,525 --> 00:00:46,362
Reports say it wanted thirty billion,

29
00:00:46,638 --> 00:00:47,875
at one point four trillion.

30
00:00:48,288 --> 00:00:50,838
Zitron even found it odd that one Bloomberg

31
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:53,425
report stressed the money had actually been wired

32
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:54,200
and received.

33
00:00:54,612 --> 00:00:56,400
In years of reading funding news,

34
00:00:56,775 --> 00:00:58,462
he says, he'd never seen that.

35
00:00:58,875 --> 00:01:00,075
And OpenAI's numbers,

36
00:01:00,275 --> 00:01:01,050
as he cites them,

37
00:01:01,338 --> 00:01:01,900
are rough.

38
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:04,525
A loss of ten point nine billion dollars

39
00:01:04,537 --> 00:01:05,287
in one quarter,

40
00:01:05,662 --> 00:01:07,588
on about ten billion dollars of revenue.

41
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,938
Yes, its margins are improving:

42
00:01:10,325 --> 00:01:12,438
from around minus one hundred fifty percent,

43
00:01:12,738 --> 00:01:14,162
to around minus one hundred.

44
00:01:14,588 --> 00:01:16,788
And its newest model got a cold reception,

45
00:01:17,188 --> 00:01:18,812
even from its usual cheerleaders.

46
00:01:19,238 --> 00:01:22,012
He expects OpenAI to need more money early

47
00:01:22,025 --> 00:01:22,588
next year.

48
00:01:23,012 --> 00:01:24,262
But its biggest backers,

49
00:01:24,362 --> 00:01:26,700
he says, chipped in only a few hundred

50
00:01:26,712 --> 00:01:27,663
million this time,

51
00:01:27,950 --> 00:01:29,925
because they're short on cash themselves.

52
00:01:30,338 --> 00:01:31,525
So his question is blunt.

53
00:01:31,938 --> 00:01:34,262
After Anthropic soaked up this much money,

54
00:01:34,625 --> 00:01:36,238
who's left to fund OpenAI?

55
00:01:36,650 --> 00:01:38,613
And the biggest supplier of all just went

56
00:01:38,625 --> 00:01:40,000
quiet on something important.
